{"name":"Apricot Iced Tea","hex":"#fbbe99","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apricot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round sweet and juicy stone fruit, resembling peach or plum in taste, with a yellow-orange flesh, lightly fuzzy skin and a large seed inside.","The apricot tree, Prunus armeniaca."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a pale yellowish-orange colour, like that of an apricot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apricot"},{"term":"iced","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With ice added.","Very cold, but not necessarily containing ice."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of ice"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iced"},{"term":"tea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Temiar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tea plant (Camellia sinensis);  a variety of this plant.","The dried leaves or buds of the tea plant;  a variety of such leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iced tea","blocks":[{"text":"You guys got iced tea? Iced tea is a form of cold tea. Though it is usually served in a glass with ice, it can refer to any tea that has been chilled or cooled. It may be sweetened with sugar or syrup, or remain unsweetened. Iced tea is also a popular packaged drink, normally mixed with fruit-flavored syrup such as lemon and peach."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Iced_Tea_from_flickr.jpg/330px-Iced_Tea_from_flickr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iced_tea","wikidata":"Q348958"},{"title":"Apricot","blocks":[{"text":"An apricot is a fruit, or the tree that bears the fruit, of several species in the genus Prunus. Usually an apricot is from the species Prunus armeniaca, but the fruits of the other species in Prunus sect. Armeniaca are also called apricots. In 2023, world production of apricots was 3.7 million tonnes, led by Turkey with 20% of the total."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Apricot_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot","wikidata":"Q3733836"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"},{"title":"Apricot (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Apricot is a light yellowish-orangish color that is similar to the color of apricots. However, it is paler than actual apricots."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apricot_(color)","wikidata":"Q1324818"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Es_Teh_Sereh_Madu-2.jpg/500px-Es_Teh_Sereh_Madu-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Es_Teh_Sereh_Madu-2.jpg/1280px-Es_Teh_Sereh_Madu-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Es_Teh_Sereh_Madu-2.jpg/500px-Es_Teh_Sereh_Madu-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Es teh serai in Indonesia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEs_Teh_Sereh_Madu-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.